@host = https://localhost:7288

### 1. Register Organiser (change the email if you run this twice: a repeat gives 409)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Organiser",
  "email": "organiser20@raceday.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": "Organiser",
  "organisationName": "RaceDay Events"
}

### 2. Login Organiser (the token is reused by the requests below)
# @name orgLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "organiser10@raceday.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 3. Get Organiser profile
GET {{host}}/api/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{orgLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 4. Create event (eventType must be Run, Walk or Cycle)
# @name createEvent
POST {{host}}/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{orgLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventName": "Centurion Sunrise Run",
  "eventType": "Run",
  "eventDate": "2027-10-15",
  "location": "Centurion, Gauteng",
  "description": "A community road running event."
}

### 5. Add a category to the event
# @name createCategory
POST {{host}}/api/events/{{createEvent.response.body.$.eventId}}/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{orgLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryName": "10km Road Race",
  "distanceKM": 10,
  "maxParticipants": 200,
  "entryFee": 150
}

### 6. Browse events (public, no token needed)
GET {{host}}/api/events

### 7. Register Participant
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Participant",
  "email": "participant20@raceday.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": "Participant",
  "dateOfBirth": "1995-05-24",
  "emergencyContact": "082 555 0102"
}

### 8. Login Participant
# @name partLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "participant10@raceday.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 9. Participant enrols in the category
# @name enrol
POST {{host}}/api/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.categoryId}}/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{partLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 10. Organiser views enrolments for the event
GET {{host}}/api/events/{{createEvent.response.body.$.eventId}}/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{orgLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 11. Organiser captures the result
POST {{host}}/api/enrolments/{{enrol.response.body.$.enrolmentId}}/result
Authorization: Bearer {{orgLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "finishTime": "00:52:30",
  "position": 14,
  "status": "Finished"
}

### 12. Participant views their own result
GET {{host}}/api/enrolments/{{enrol.response.body.$.enrolmentId}}/result
Authorization: Bearer {{partLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 13. Participant performance history
GET {{host}}/api/participants/me/history
Authorization: Bearer {{partLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 14. Role check: a Participant must NOT create events (expect 403)
POST {{host}}/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{partLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventName": "Should fail",
  "eventType": "Run",
  "eventDate": "2027-10-15",
  "location": "Nowhere"
}

### 15. Role check: an Organiser must NOT enrol (expect 403)
POST {{host}}/api/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.categoryId}}/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{orgLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 16. No token at all (expect 401)
GET {{host}}/api/profile
